{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/121276-another-reason-why-some-changelings-probably-wouldn-t-want-to-escape","id":121276,"title":"Another reason why some Changelings probably wouldn't want to escape.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-28T16:07:03-07:00","id":121276,"title":"Another reason why some Changelings probably wouldn't want to escape.","content":"I saw this and it made me think of something. What if, during their durance, some Changelings haven't forgotten their mortal lives, and yet wouldn't leave because their normal lives back home are actually WORSE than the mercurial politics of the Gentry.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/this-dark-short-film-reveals-peter-pans-depressing-orig-1568824603\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/this-dark-short-film-...rig-1568824603</a><br /> <br /> It would be Clarity rending for some if they return to the Hell that's their mortal lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T19:43:44-07:00","id":123577,"title":"","content":"If the character never escapes Faerie, then there's really no point of playing the game. That's likely a little too slavish to the game's set up, though, so let me try to look at it differently...<br /> <br /> The point is kind of a conceit of the game. That is, only those who WANT to return wind up returning, and only those who return become the Lost. If the durance were pleasant or better than the life one left behind, then the term 'durance' would hardly apply. Of course, the game does not ever say that such a story is outside the realm of possible character experience. Some changelings do become Loyalists, after all, working for the very same monsters who inflicted bondage. I don't think that's what you're getting at, though.<br /> <br /> There's a possibility that one of the Lost could have returned from Faerie without any effort on her own part, just being dumped back into the 'mundane' world, for reasons that the changeling cannot understand. What does that DO to a soul? Maybe the character works to make the hellish world she returned to better, or maybe she seeks ways to rum away from it.<br /> <br /> Take for example Tommy Two-Tips, who is by every possible definition one of the Fairest. Tommy does not want for attention, rarely is excluded, has everything that many of his fellows would consider an ideal life, yet it feels like hell to him. You see, his mistress in Faerie, only known as the Lover, gave Tommy everything he would ever want, an all-encompassing, perfect smothering love. How did he get back? His best guess is that he was sent from from her side, expelled from her heavenly presence because her caprice or for some crime he does not remember committing. Maybe he wants to go back. Maybe he'll try to get back by any means he can manage. However he looks at it, his life away from her is hell, though he has no idea how he might return to her. He's most definitely not one of the Loyalist faction, but Tommy's longing for the Lover's attentions remains a hole inside him that cannot be filled. That said, a part of him knows that if she DID send him away, the Lover would not likely take him back, and as painful as the possibility of her spurning him is, he cannot bear the prospect of KNOWING that she spurned him.<br /> <br /> ...I really like the idea of turning the game's basic premises on their heads, and it's quite possible to make such things work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T00:36:52-07:00","id":123651,"title":"","content":"Part of what you mention is one of the elements of Victorian Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T02:28:47-07:00","id":123682,"title":"","content":"Peter Pan is definitely a True Fae, kidnapping children because he believes he is saving them from the nightmare of growing into adults, and from their unhappy lives back home.<br /> <br /> Those who can escape from his Durance are those who realize how much of his philosophy stems from his own disappointment with life back at home. (And his jealous feelings towards his younger baby brother who he thought his parents had to replace him, as seen in one of the books.)<br /> <br /> You could perhaps run a Changeling game where Tinkerbell is revealed to be the real villain, who &quot;freed&quot; Peter from his life back home and she's training him to grow into another True Fae. If the players manage to uncover Peter's secret and convince him to return to the real world with them, Tinkerbell will reveal her true identity and try to stop them from leaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T17:48:35-07:00","id":129437,"title":"","content":"There is a real difference between not wanting to leave your durance and being forced out of it. The latter doesn't even have to mean Privateer, frankly. Why? Because said person might have enjoyed their time, but hearing the horrors others suffered not want THEM to go back. Just wants back personally, into the situation they were in. <br /> <br /> There is just as much angst in the exile from heaven as there is in the escape from hell, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T18:17:37-07:00","id":129465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/121276-another-reason-why-some-changelings-probably-wouldn-t-want-to-escape?p=123682#post123682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Peter Pan is definitely a True Fae, kidnapping children because he believes he is saving them from the nightmare of growing into adults, and from their unhappy lives back home.<br /> <br /> Those who can escape from his Durance are those who realize how much of his philosophy stems from his own disappointment with life back at home. (And his jealous feelings towards his younger baby brother who he thought his parents had to replace him, as seen in one of the books.)<br /> <br /> You could perhaps run a Changeling game where Tinkerbell is revealed to be the real villain, who &quot;freed&quot; Peter from his life back home and she's training him to grow into another True Fae. If the players manage to uncover Peter's secret and convince him to return to the real world with them, Tinkerbell will reveal her true identity and try to stop them from leaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to go too far off topic, but Peter was most definitely born to human parents in the human world and taken to Neverland by Tinkerbell. He actually talks about how he ran away because he overheard his parents talking about what he would be when he grew up and it scared him, and how Tink found him, a lone, lost baby, and &quot;saved&quot; him. So you'd have to make a few changes for Peter-as-a-True-Fae to work, but your latter interpretation is not only canon-friendly, it's pretty much the actual plot of book. I mean, what does Tinkerbell try to do when Wendy comes into Peter's life, threatening to give him a connection in the human world potentially worth going back for? She tries to kill Wendy. Multiple times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-09-2014, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T22:59:18-07:00","id":142111,"title":"","content":"Or that's just the story Peter tells. It's not like there's any witnesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}